000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. SORTRET.
000300* SORT-RETURN is the sort's return code, stored when the SORT
000400* ends. IKFCBL00 ignores a value the program moves there: 16 set
000500* in the input procedure does not stop the RELEASEs after it, and
000600* 16 set in the output procedure does not stop the RETURNs.
000700* RETURN here has no INTO. Expected output recorded from IBM ANS
000800* COBOL on TK5.
000900 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001000 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001100 FILE-CONTROL.
001200     SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-SORTWK01.
001300 DATA DIVISION.
001400 FILE SECTION.
001500 SD  SORT-FILE.
001600 01  S-REC.
001700     05  S-K PIC 99.
001800     05  S-X PIC X(38).
001900 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002000 01  SR PIC S9(4).
002100 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
002200 MAIN-PARA.
002300     SORT SORT-FILE ASCENDING KEY S-K
002400         INPUT PROCEDURE IS IN-STOP OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS OUT-STOP.
002500     MOVE SORT-RETURN TO SR. DISPLAY 'AFTER THE SORT ' SR.
002600     STOP RUN.
002700 IN-STOP SECTION.
002800 I1.
002900     MOVE 3 TO S-K. MOVE 'THREE' TO S-X. RELEASE S-REC.
003000     MOVE 16 TO SORT-RETURN.
003100     DISPLAY 'IN-STOP SET 16'.
003200     MOVE 1 TO S-K. MOVE 'ONE' TO S-X. RELEASE S-REC.
003300     DISPLAY 'IN-STOP AFTER SECOND RELEASE'.
003400     MOVE 2 TO S-K. MOVE 'TWO' TO S-X. RELEASE S-REC.
003500     DISPLAY 'IN-STOP AFTER THIRD RELEASE'.
003600 OUT-STOP SECTION.
003700 O1.
003800     RETURN SORT-FILE AT END
003900         DISPLAY 'OUT-STOP AT END' GO TO O-EXIT.
004000     DISPLAY 'OUT GOT ' S-K ' ' S-X.
004100     MOVE 16 TO SORT-RETURN.
004200     GO TO O1.
004300 O-EXIT.
004400     EXIT.
